  "note": "Printed-only assertions. No new wiring: p.81 says 'Without changing the program from experiment 8' and p.80 ends 'Leave this program wired on your MINIVAC for experiment 9.', so wires = as_printed = the Experiment 8 table, image-read against PDF p.86 (67 wires, 17/17/17/16 columns) and matching programs.json wiresEffective; ER-25 (p.80) and ER-26 (p.82) are prose only and change no wire, so errata_applied is empty. Slide switch RIGHT = 0 (target 1000), LEFT = 1 (target 0), from the p.80 convention 'A slide switch RIGHT represents 0; a slide switch LEFT represents 1.' Script follows the p.82 worked example 110 x 1010: switches all RIGHT, pushbuttons 4 and 5 held, release, enter the recorded number on the switches, then each left shift is done by hand in the p.80 order (switch 1 takes switch 2's position, ... switch 5 takes switch 6's, switch 6 to zero) with a settle after each move. A 1 s advance precedes each expect because settle returns on contacts while a lamp that just went out is still 'dim'. Asserted: 000110 with pushbuttons 4 and 5 held, 001100 after the first shift, 011000 after the second, 011110 with pushbuttons 4 and 5 held again, and 111100 after the last shift. The last reading is printed twice as '11100' (the shift result and 'the final result: 11100 or 60'); errata ER-26 says 'decimal 60 is 111100 in binary. It is written incorrectly in two places.', and the page itself prints '110 X 1010 = 111100'; the expect asserts the erratum's 111100 and quotes both. Not asserted: the lamp state after each 'enter the number which you recorded in the slide switches' step (the p.80 rule 'The number is now displayed in the binary output lights' would apply, but p.82 states no reading there), and 'The limit of this accumulator is 111111 (63).' (a capacity claim with no input sequence).",
